A||||3||ToddAsh||Cat Removal||||5||
Z||000000||ToddAsh||01-26-2001||10:56 PM||||Does the V6 sound much better with the Cat removed.I was going to change the whole exhaust system but I hate to because I only have 15,000 miles on the car and the pipes and Muffler look new.I'd just like it louder.Just put Classic tags on so no more emission inspection. Thanks, Todd||||reg||5
Z||000001||theogre||01-26-2001||11:23 PM||||No more inspection doesn't make it legal. Also. PA is still in dispute with USEPA. Don't count on that exemption lasting forever. PA getting fed highway money is at stake.<P>removing the cat won't likely make it louder by much. Screwing with the exhaust w/o knowing what you are doing can actually cost you HP and/or torque. Louder isn't always better. Sleepers are more fun. Get'em before they know what hit'em.<P>Knowing most of PA is still rural, even Philly cops have a rural mentality most of the time, all you are doing by making it louder is make yourself a ticket magnet. DE NJ and NY just love noisy out of state cars. MD is even more flakey than PA. But then having to deal with Baltimore and D.C. would make anyone nuts.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Black88GT||01-26-2001||11:30 PM||||I have a Borla exhaust with no cat.  It's pretty quiet at idle, but you can tell whats there (or not there for that matter) when you lay on it.  It doesn't sound NEARLY as loud as all those rice boys running around with their Greddy exhausts, so I am not worried about cops.  I am also not worried about emissions, I can give the guy 100 bucks at the station in the city and he will pass me (done it with 3 cars already).  It's good for 2 years and I got it done in September.  So even if that guy isn't there or I can't get anyone to do it, I'll just throw on a cat for the time being, no biggie.<P>I would recommend Rodney Dickmans 304 stainless steel pipe if you are going to do it.<BR><P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>'88 GT t-top 3.4<BR>Baltimore, MD<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/cartmanico.gif">             <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/kennyico.gif">           <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/stanico.gif">         <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/kyleico.gif">             <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/chefico.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||ToddAsh||01-26-2001||11:46 PM||||In Pa. Antique and Classics are emission exempt.I won't worry about my little Fiero polluting until the trucks and busses do.The police around here don't care if my cars growl a little,hell their mostly family.Ha Ha. Thanks,Todd||||reg||1
